For deck review with the SlidePix MCP server:

1. Call `list_slides` with an absolute deck path unless slide IDs are already
   known.
2. Call `inspect_slides` for exact element, transition, timeline, and notes
   metadata.
3. Call `render_slides` for visual feedback. Prefer a single image contact sheet
   for several slides; specify row/column/grid only when it improves comparison.
4. Cite slide IDs or 1-based indices in feedback so fixes are unambiguous.

These tools are read-only. Never claim that an MCP call changed a deck. If a
render fails because Chromium is missing, ask the user to run **SlidePix:
Configure MCP** or **SlidePix: Install Export Renderer** in VS Code/Cursor.

When changing MCP code, read @docs/modules/mcp.md and preserve the mutation and
asset-containment boundaries in @architecture.md.

